// INTERPRETATION GUIDE
// ============================================================
//
// CASE A:
//
// Trees ↓
// NDVI ↓
// MNDWI ↑
//
// → strongest support for transition from
//   tree-dominated vegetation toward wetter /
//   inundated / water-associated conditions.
//
//
//
// CASE B:
//
// Trees ↓
// NDVI ↓
// MNDWI ≈ stable
//
// → vegetation degradation / canopy reduction
//   may be more plausible than inundation.
//
//
//
// CASE C:
//
// Trees ↓
// NDVI ≈ stable
// MNDWI ↑
//
// → vegetation may still be present,
//   but surface wetness / inundation increased.
//
//
//
// CASE D:
//
// Trees ↓↓↓
// NDVI ≈ stable
// MNDWI ≈ stable
//
// → Dynamic World class-probability instability
//   becomes a stronger possibility.
//
//
//
// IMPORTANT:
//
// NDVI and MNDWI are supporting indicators,
// not direct proof of disturbance cause.
//
// Coastal tidal conditions,
// soil moisture,
// seasonal variation,
// composite dates,
// and cloud masking
// can influence both indices.
